  "id": "CP03Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Outpatient defibrillator (ICD) replacement",
  "description": "An implantable cardioverter-defibrillator (ICD) replacement involves removing your old device and implanting a new one under your skin. An ICD is a small device that monitors your heart rhythm and delivers an electric shock if dangerous irregular heartbeats develop, potentially saving your life. Your doctor performs this outpatient procedure in a cardiac electrophysiology lab while you're under local anesthesia. The new device is programmed to your specific needs. This type of procedure can involve removal and revision of the device, and the cost may vary depending on the specific service performed.",
